# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this Next.js 14 App Router project.

## Implementation Details

### 1. Fetched Latest Documentation
Retrieved the most up-to-date installation instructions from the official Vercel documentation:
- URL: https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart
- Framework: Next.js App Router (v13.5+)

### 2. Package Installation
Installed the `@vercel/speed-insights` package:
- Package: `@vercel/speed-insights@^2.0.0`
- Method: npm install
- Added to dependencies in package.json

### 3. Configuration Changes

**Modified Files:**
- `app/layout.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights component to root layout

**Changes Made:**
1. Added import statement:
   ```tsx
   import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";
   ```

2. Added component to the layout:
   ```tsx
   <body className="antialiased bg-white">
     {children}
     <SpeedInsights />
   </body>
   ```

### 4. Verification
- ✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
- ✅ No TypeScript errors
- ✅ Next.js production build generated without issues
- ✅ Package lock file updated (package-lock.json)

### 5. Framework-Specific Notes
- Using Next.js v14.2.35 (App Router)
- No additional configuration required for this Next.js version
- SpeedInsights component automatically integrates with Next.js
- Component placed after {children} as per official documentation
- Uses `@vercel/speed-insights/next` import for Next.js v13.5+

## Next Steps
Once deployed to Vercel, Speed Insights will automatically begin tracking:
- Core Web Vitals (LCP, FID, CLS)
- Time to First Byte (TTFB)
- First Contentful Paint (FCP)
- Other performance metrics

The analytics will be available in the Vercel dashboard under the Speed Insights tab.

## Files Changed
1. `app/layout.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights import and component
2. `package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
3. `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package dependencies
